Negative control for the HANDOFF control (C1/C2).

Strips the handoff branch from both the availability gate and the click, so a
declared `edit`/`add` control falls back to calling a live action of the same
name — which is exactly C2's defect: Add fires `ensure()` with no address to
create, no form is ever presented, and Edit has nothing to call at all.

Apply from the repo root: `git apply <this file>`; revert with `git apply -R`.

Reds: the add/edit specs — the editor must OPEN (and only where its target is
registered), never call a collection action.

